## Test Data Fixtures

```javascript
// tests/fixtures/telemetryPayload.js
const baseTelemetry = {
  t: 4632,
  fuel_l: 2.93,
  fuel_pct: 4,
  engine: true,
  door: true,
  temp_c: 22.0,
  accel_g: -2.71,
  speed_kmh: 5.9,
  rate_lhr: 0.00,
  trip_sec: 0,
  fuel_used: 0.00,
  lat: 9.0320,
  lon: 38.7469,
  location: 'Home',
  geofence_ok: true,
  low_fuel: true,
  parking: false,
  overspeed: false,
  alert: 'Low fuel warning'
};

// Use spread to override specific fields in tests
const engineOff = { ...baseTelemetry, engine: false, speed_kmh: 0 };
const overspeedPayload = { ...baseTelemetry, speed_kmh: 95, overspeed: true };
const parkingMode = { ...baseTelemetry, engine: false, parking: true, speed_kmh: 0 };

module.exports = { baseTelemetry, engineOff, overspeedPayload, parkingMode };
```

---

## Running Tests

```bash
# Unit tests
npm run test:unit

# Integration tests
npm run test:integration

# Smoke tests (requires running server)
SMOKE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000 npm run test:smoke

# All tests with coverage
npm run test:coverage

# Watch mode during development
npm run test:watch
```

```json
// package.json scripts
{
  "test": "jest",
  "test:unit": "jest tests/unit --coverage",
  "test:integration": "jest tests/integration --coverage",
  "test:smoke": "jest tests/smoke --testTimeout=10000",
  "test:coverage": "jest --coverage --coverageReporters=text-summary",
  "test:watch": "jest --watch"
}
```

---

## PR Test Checklist

Every PR that touches logic MUST include:

- [ ] Unit tests for every new/modified service function
- [ ] Unit tests for every new/modified validator
- [ ] Integration tests for every new/modified route
- [ ] Smoke test for every new endpoint
- [ ] Coverage does not drop below thresholds
- [ ] No test uses `console.log` in assertion (use `expect`)
- [ ] No test has `.only` or `.skip` in committed code
- [ ] Fixtures in `tests/fixtures/` not duplicated inline